Z||000000||V8Fiero||09-02-2001||01:46 AM||||I know that there has been some talk about using contact paper for the fascias in the car. <P>Well, I was strolling through Wally world this evening and decided to try this little trick. I have an extra dash and radio fascia to experiment on. I bought a roll of Cherry wood paper.<P>After about an hour and a half of careful trimming with a SHARP, SHARP, did I say sharp? razor blade, I was pretty impressed with the results. Unless you get nose to the fascia, you cant really tell that its contact paper.<P>Im gonna put the test panels in my car tomorrow and see how they look. If I like the look, I will do the rest of the cars panels.<P>Just thought I would pass this information along<P>Thanks for reading<BR>Scott<P>------------------<BR>86 SE Gold<BR>86 GT Red <BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/RedRavensig.JPG"> <BR>"Trying to change from V8Fiero to RedRavenGT"||||reg||1
