Z||000008||AusFiero||09-02-2001||09:14 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Haze_Performance:<BR><B> <BR>They do... <BR> <A HREF="http://www.tapeworks.com/Pages/carbonlook.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.tapeworks.com/Pages/carbonlook.html</A> <P>&<P>Rally<BR>5255 Northwest 159th st.<BR>Miami, FL. 33014<P>Xtreme FX Interior Design Film (48"x18")<BR>part#19960<P>$19.41 shipped<P>1-800-227-2559<P>Here a few pics of this kind.. <A HREF="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=99075&a=723601&p=18231068&Sequence=1" TARGET=_blank>http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=99075&a=723601&p=18231068&Sequence=1</A>  <A HREF="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=99075&a=723601&p=18231071&Sequence=1" TARGET=_blank>http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=99075&a=723601&p=18231071&Sequence=1</A>  <A HREF="http://www.fieroproject.com/cf.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fieroproject.com/cf.html</A> <P>(Above pics belong to DXR DAD)<P><BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>You got that slightly wrong Haze, well by their web site anyway. The 2 pieces for $19.95 is 10" X 14" X 2 which is not enough to do a complete Fiero Kit. You would need their 14" X 40" roll to do a complete Fiero consisting of dash face (13"X7"), heater/stereo  surround face (10"X10"), centre console section (9"X11") and GT Gauge Pod (9"X3"). That costs $39.95.<P>All bracketed dimensions are allowing for overlap to wrap around the edge like I have done mine, or you can trim them to reveal the bevelled edges. <BR>Also you have to allow for all the patten to be running in the one direction to look right.<P><BR><P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.jadeweb.com.au/fiero/ausfiero1.gif">   <BR><A HREF="http://www.jadeweb.com.au/fiero" TARGET=_blank>My Fiero</A> | <A HREF="http://www.fieroshop.com.au" TARGET=_blank>Fiero Accessories</A>||202.139.20.3||reg||1
